  "blocks": {
    "\"No, schema migration — keep it human-in-the-loop. I want to see each step and steer if it picks the wrong column to backfill from.\"": "“不行，这是 schema 迁移，要保持人工介入。我需要看到每一步；如果它选错用于回填的列，可以立即纠正。”",
    "\"Run this AFK overnight?\"": "“让它整夜 AFK 运行？”",
    "A working pattern where one or more humans pair with the agent during a session — reviewing, redirecting, or collaborating in real time. The human is present and engaged, not just gating individual actions.": "人工介入是一种工作模式：一个或多个人在<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/session\">会话</a>期间与<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agent\">智能体</a>协作，实时审查、纠正方向或共同完成工作。人始终在场并积极参与，而不只是为单个操作充当审批门。",
    "Some work is in-the-loop by nature, because your reactions are the input. Grilling only works with you there to answer the questions; prototyping only works with you there to react to the artifact.": "某些工作天然需要人工介入，因为你的反应本身就是输入。<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/grilling\">深度追问</a>需要你在场回答问题；<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/prototyping\">原型设计</a>也需要你在场对产物作出反馈。",
    "Staying in the loop costs your attention, which is the scarce resource. Part of getting better with agents is moving more work safely out of the loop — with plans, automated checks, and human review at the end instead of supervision throughout.": "保持人工介入会消耗人的注意力，而注意力才是稀缺资源。提高智能体使用能力的一部分，就是通过计划、<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/automated-check\">自动化检查</a>和最终的<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/human-review\">人工审查</a>，把更多工作安全地移出实时监督过程。",
    "The contrast is with AFK work, where the agent runs unattended and you judge the result afterwards. Human-in-the-loop means catching problems while they're still cheap: you see the agent reach for the wrong file, misread the requirement, or start down a dead end, and you redirect it in one sentence — rather than discovering twenty minutes of confident work built on that mistake. Agents don't reliably know when they're off track; left alone, they tend to push forward rather than stop and ask.": "它与 <a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/afk\">AFK</a> 工作相对：AFK 中智能体无人值守运行，你在结束后再评判结果；人工介入则在问题成本仍低时及时发现。你看到智能体打开错误文件、误解需求或走向死路，可以用一句话立刻纠正，而不是 20 分钟后才发现它已经围绕错误自信地完成大量工作。智能体并不能可靠判断自己何时偏离方向；无人干预时，它们往往会继续向前，而不是停下来提问。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>",
    "Which pattern fits depends on the work. Well-specified, low-risk, easy-to-verify tasks suit AFK. Tasks that are ambiguous, irreversible, or where you'd struggle to review the finished result — a schema migration, a tricky design decision, anything touching production — suit staying in the loop. The judgement call is essentially: how expensive is a wrong turn, and how late would you catch it?": "选择哪种模式取决于工作性质。定义清晰、风险较低、容易验证的任务适合 AFK；存在歧义、不可逆，或最终结果难以审查的任务——例如 schema 迁移、棘手设计决策、任何涉及生产环境的改动——更适合保留人工介入。判断的核心问题是：走错一步的代价有多高，以及你会多晚才发现？"
  },
